Usage: copilot plugin uninstall <name>

Uninstall a plugin.

Removes a previously installed plugin and its associated skills.

Arguments:
  <name>
          Plugin name (plugin-name or plugin-name@marketplace-name)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Examples:
  # Uninstall a marketplace plugin
  $ copilot plugin uninstall arch@awesome-copilot

  # Uninstall a directly installed plugin
  $ copilot plugin uninstall my-plugin

Learn More:
  Use `copilot <command> --help` for more information about a command.
  Read the documentation at https://docs.github.com/copilot/how-tos/copilot-cli
